有些担忧，因为在模型变强之前，也就是 12 月那个……冬天之前，我一直在和这些模型打交道，那时候情况还没变得这么好。
scared because I'd been working with models you know, just before they were good and before the December uh winter where you know

439
00:41:03,918 --> 00:41:14,288
所以我感受到了以前工作时的那些限制。我知道，比如你给智能体提供的上下文越多，它的表现就越差。
uh things got really good. And so I was I felt the constraints from what I'd been working with before. I knew that, for instance, the more context you put you give to the agent, the worse it performs.

440
00:41:14,734 --> 00:41:21,648
我知道你在播客上邀请过 Dex Horthy，Dex 对我影响很大，尤其是他关于“智能区”和“低智区”的理念。
I know you had Dex Horthy on this podcast, and Dex um is a really big influence on me, especially his idea of the smart zone and the dumb zone.

441
00:41:23,088 --> 00:41:28,928
是的。所以这个概念就是……为了让你不用去完整听那期播客，虽然你确实应该去听。
Yeah. So idea of that just to kind of um so you don't have to go and listen to that podcast in full, although you should.

442
00:41:29,568 --> 00:41:35,808
基本上来说，你给智能体的上下文越多，每一个标记都在争夺注意力。
You have essentially the more context you give to the agent, every token is shouting for attention.

443
00:41:36,592 --> 00:41:41,472
房间里声音越多，就越难听到那些重要的声音。
And the more voices you put into that room, the harder it is to hear the important ones.

444
00:41:41,742 --> 00:41:46,532
因此模型开始丢失事物之间的联系，并因此产生错误。
And so the model starts losing the connections between things and making mistakes because of that.

445
00:41:46,992 --> 00:41:55,152
你可以把它看作是一种缓慢的退化，但在上下文窗口中，有些部分表现更好，有些则更差。
And you can think of that as a slow decline, but there is a portion of the context window where it's better and where it's worse.

446
00:41:55,232 --> 00:42:01,232
所以你有了“智能区”，目前我认为，对于前沿模型来说，大约是前 150,000 个标记。
And so you have the smart zone, which is currently, I would say, about the first 150,000 tokens of frontier models.

447
00:42:01,792 --> 00:42:03,312
在 100 万个标记的窗口中。
Of a 1 million token window.

448
00:42:03,632 --> 00:42:03,792
没错。
Yep.

449
00:42:03,952 --> 00:42:08,032
无论是什么尺寸的标记窗口。不论什么尺寸，所以上下文窗口的大小并不重要。
Of any size token window. Of any size, so doesn't it doesn't matter the context window size.

450
00:42:08,238 --> 00:42:11,952
关键在于原始的标记数量，即原始的注意力关系。
It's all about raw amount of tokens, raw amount of attention relationships.

451
00:42:12,174 --> 00:42:15,556
然后剩下的部分就会变得越来越差，越来越糟。
And then the rest of it will slowly degrade more and more and more.

452
00:42:15,982 --> 00:42:26,468
于是我开始思考：如何处理那些超过 15 万个标记的工作（这并不算多），并把它们分摊到多个上下文窗口、多个会话中？
And so I started thinking: how do I take work that's bigger than 150k tokens, which is not very large, and portion it out over multiple context windows, multiple sessions?

453
00:42:26,926 --> 00:42:31,472
这让我尝试了很多次，用各种不同的方法反复琢磨。
And this took me a lot of tries, a lot of different fiddling around with different approaches.

454
00:42:31,758 --> 00:42:39,872
Raphael循环就是其中一种方案。Raphael循环旨在最大化利用智能区，因为它们本质上只是给 Raphael loop 一个目标，并告诉它：
The Ralph Loops was one version of that. Ralph loops are designed to make the most of the smart zone because they essentially just give the Ralph loop a goal and they say,

455
00:42:40,112 --> 00:42:47,072
做出能让我们更接近目标的最小变动，然后清空你的上下文。接着清空上下文，重新开始。没错。
do the smallest possible change that will get us further towards that goal and then clear your context. And then clear the context, start from fresh. Exactly.

456
00:42:47,246 --> 00:42:50,112
而且你并不是在技术层面上从零开始，因为你拥有代码库，对吧？
And you're not technically starting from fresh because you've got the code base, right?

457
00:42:50,432 --> 00:42:55,588
文件系统和环境中保留了一点状态，但本质上模型里没有。
There's a little bit of state saved in the file system and in the environment, but not in the model, essentially.

458
00:42:55,918 --> 00:43:03,872
这就是核心思路。所以我开始思考，如何把这个 Raphael Loop 的想法变得更稳定一点，并把它转化成技能？
So that's the idea. So I started thinking, how do I take that Ralph Loop idea, but make it a little bit more stable and turn that into skills?

459
00:43:04,238 --> 00:43:07,332
于是我意识到我需要两种不同类型的文档。
And so what I realized I needed was two different types of documents.

460
00:43:07,630 --> 00:43:11,552
你需要一份关于你要去往何处的文档，也就是目标文档。
You need a document for where you're going, which is the destination document.

461
00:43:11,952 --> 00:43:15,952
我以前管它叫产品需求文档，现在我称之为规范。
I used to call that a product requirements document or a spec is what I call it now.

462
00:43:16,352 --> 00:43:19,472
这就是声明你何时到达终点的规范。
So that's the specification that declares when you've reached the end.

463
00:43:19,662 --> 00:43:24,388
然后你需要把这个规范分解成一个个的任务单，每个会话对应一个任务单。
And then you need to break that spec down into individual tickets, one ticket per session.

464
00:43:25,070 --> 00:43:29,060
所以我有一个非常简单的技能，就是先进行规范化，然后再生成任务单。
And so I'd have a very simple skill, just to spec and then to tickets.

465
00:43:29,614 --> 00:43:33,188
所以你把你之前进行的“ grilling”环节转化成一份规范。
And so you take that grilling session that you've had and you turn it into a spec.

466
00:43:33,632 --> 00:43:42,352
现在这个规范可以涵盖 30、40 个甚至更多的任务单，这意味着你可以有非常庞大的一整块工作内容，而且它们都关联到这个规范中。
now that spec can work over you know 30, 40 tickets, let's say you can have really massive, great big chunks of work that are all tied into that spec.

467
00:43:42,638 --> 00:43:51,712
这就是核心思路。你先进行 grilling，把 grilling 的结果变成一份规范，然后对这些任务单运行某种执行者循环，直到完成一大块工作。
And so that's the main idea. You just grill, you turn that grilling into a spec, and then you just run some kind of implementer loop over those tickets until you've got a huge chunk of work.

