A related point I want to emphasize is the importance of leading words with AI.

1035
01:35:18,640 --> 01:35:25,920
当 Matt 开始使用诸如「追踪子弹」或「垂直切片」等术语时，模型在规划中就开始更好地遵循他的思路了。
When Matt started to use terms like tracer bullet or vertical slices, the model started to follow his ideas better in planning.

1036
01:35:26,281 --> 01:35:34,528
仔细想想，这很有道理，因为软件工程文献是 LLM 训练的一部分，所以这些术语也是模型先验知识的一部分。
And If you think about it, this makes sense, because software engineering literature is part of LLM training, so these terms are also part of the models priors.

1037
01:35:34,768 --> 01:35:39,248
同样有趣的是，用正确的词汇来描述你的问题并不是个新概念。
Just as interestingly, using the right words for describing your problem is not a new concept.

1038
01:35:39,408 --> 01:35:47,568
例如，当我邀请 Ken Beck 来参加播客时，他提到 30 或 35 年前，他和 Ward Cunningham 的桌上放着一本同义词词典，
